. The other heaters are still hot (C6 66.5, C8 73.9, C3 448.5). That points to heater H706 being off or failed. In a normal run the column temperatures climb; they don't fall like this.\n\nI didn't give a precise second because there are no raw readings around the likely onset. It is probably near second 0, but only the map's averages cover that period."}, {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01U1PfaKbnGuPADjLGU7P5qP", "name": "report", "input": {"state": "anomalous", "onset": {"kind": "earlier_than", "second": 2150}, "cause": "Heater H706 (C001) appears off or failed and is cooling smoothly from the start of the record. Its temperature is now below the column process temperature.", "evidence": [{"channel": "C7", "start": 0, "end": 3949, "observation": "600 s means 60.25 -> 44.49; each drop is about 2/3 of the previous one, a single cooling curve that began at or before second 0"}, {"channel": "C7", "start": 2150, "end": 3949, "observation": "Raw readings fall smoothly from 48.2 to 44.3 with no break, so the onset is not in this window"}]}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8056, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1254, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1226, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 456}, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global"}, "diagnostics": null}, "error": null}]}